+*   **Strengths:** Real-time rendering capability, view-dependent color via SH, efficient culling [S1, unofficial, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** Approximation error from Jacobian linearization (perspective distortion is not perfectly Gaussian), requires careful tuning of $\epsilon_{2d}$ and opacity thresholds [S1, unofficial, S2, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-Originated from the "3D Gaussian Splatting" paper by Kerbl et al. (2023), which introduced the representation of scenes as 3D Gaussians for efficient novel view synthesis. The projection method described here is the core rasterization technique used in implementations like the unofficial "tsplat" library and the LichtFeld-Studio reference implementation [S1, unofficial, S2, unofficial]. It builds on the mathematical foundation of projecting ellipsoids via Jacobian linearization, a technique common in computer graphics for handling perspective transforms of quadratic surfaces.
